+.. _cli_transform_schema:
+
+Applying a combined schema plan
+-------------------------------
+
+The ``transform-schema`` command applies a JSON schema plan::
+
+    sqlite-utils transform-schema data.db plan.json --dry-run
+    sqlite-utils transform-schema data.db plan.json
+
+A plan maps existing table names to operations, for example::
+
+    {
+      "products": {
+        "rename": {"name": "title"},
+        "types": {"price": "REAL"},
+        "defaults": {"price": 0.0},
+        "column_order": ["id", "name", "price"]
+      }
+    }
+
+References use original column names, including when renamed. Supported
+operations are rename, drop, types, not_null, defaults, column_order and strict.
+See :ref:`python_api_transform_schema` for complete conversion rules, supported
+schemas and transaction guarantees. The whole plan commits atomically while
+preserving dependency behavior. ``--dry-run`` performs the same validation on
+an isolated snapshot without modifying the original database. Success prints
+the final report as JSON; failure exits nonzero with an error on stderr.
+
